  "trigger": "Registered physical Train Observer cargo filter setter; ordinary RailwaySavedData graph-first/train restore; actual LevelTick.Post and block entity server tick; optional topology point invalidation/rebind.",
  "input": "World-owned point stable UUID, directed edge/position, physical block dimension/position, copied authored ItemStack filter, residual activated counter/current TrainId; loaded Train OccupiedObservers UUID set. Derived cargo-version match cache is deliberately not serialized.",
  "output": "Registered OBSERVER factory instantiates TrackObserver. EdgePointStorage disk read migration=false restores point geometry and payload before TrackGraph EdgeData resolves type+UUID references; RailwaySavedData loads all graphs before Train. Train constructor starts fresh empty filtering cache then restores OccupiedObservers; earlyTick scans every occupied detector, uses actual carriage item simulation/filter.test and fluid simulation, refreshes detector counter to8/current train UUID if matching. Physical BE tick derives POWERED and notifies neighboring block updates/display; actual Block.getSignal returns15/0. Real crossing listeners enter/leave occupied set, remove derived cache at rear; Carriage.travel invokes them with direction/front/back swaps. Changing physical filter copies stack, changes logical detector, requests train re-collection, persisted independently in BE behaviour and graph point. Optional topology migration saves whole point payload via invalidateAt; new observer read(true) skips base geometry/old block address but restores detector filter/counter/TrainId, assigns new geometry/address; blockEntityAdded then overwrites logical filter with physical BE filter and notifies. Whole authored cargo detector1, shared graph/train storage/filter codecs/timer0.",
  "preservation": "This world-installed cargo predicate controlling a real external redstone circuit is independent of per-train owned vehicle/passenger custody f729, schedule completion f550, multiwheel topology a781, selected route/wait2f248 and physical ENTRY/CROSS admission policy3977. No accepted owner is narrowed: physical signal controls section admission based on occupancy/reservation/power; this detector performs cargo predicate matching without admitting/stopping trains, and can be observed by a separate circuit across arbitrary trains. Different user cargo predicate with identical train route/signal policy changes the external output. All-status whole serialized ledger lacks original ID/method SHA/AST; TrackObserver itself had no serialized ledger occurrence during first scan. Timer, TrainId, filter variants, dimensional keys and graph wrappers give no extra credit.",
  "limits": [
    "Source-only modern NeoForge Create commit7ff2760, not same runtime/API bridge to Dynasty Forge1.20.1. No network, Java/game/world execution, production/checklist/shared-ledger changes or Git actions. Archive metadata pin/source and excerpt hashes checked, archive ZIP bytes not rehashed this turn.",
    "TrackObserver.tick ignores preTrains and GlobalRailwayManager calls points before and after trains: counter decrements twice each world tick, and earlyTick keepAlive8 is followed by post tick decrement7. Thus 8 is NOT proven8-world-tick hold. Stored positive counter can temporarily power without currently matching cargo until expiration; negative/huge counters not bounded. currentTrain cleared on nonactivated tick; read missing TrainId does not clear reused object, constructor fresh null.",
    "Fluid loop repeats tank.drain(1,SIMULATE) rather than getFluidInTank(slot), so does not prove each distinct tank is sampled. Shared wrapper drain choice may miss matching later fluid; full wrapper and fluid emptying implementation not audited. Item extraction is simulate=true but underlying external handler contracts not proven globally.",
    "Derived cache uses sum of int per-carriage versions, no predicate identity. Fresh cache default(-1,false) recomputes normally at zero; int overflow/version-sum collisions can reuse stale result. Wrapper increments only specified mutation paths, actual backing storage external/internal mutation coverage not universal. Filter change notifyTrains only flags trains with a travelling wheel on passed edge: long train straddling detector edge without wheel there may retain old match cache. No universal immediate invalidation guarantee.",
    "TrainCargoManager version not serialized. Real mounted storage restored via Carriage dimensional data; several dimensional reads share same carriage storage. Existing f729 cargo limitation remains, no lossless cargo restoration claim. MountedStorageManager catches Throwable, logs/partially retains decoded entries and initializes; unknown codecs may be omitted. Legacy mounted reader not read anew, shared existing b384 owner unchanged0.",
    "Empty filter activates any occupying train; basic item filter test=false NBT comparison, fluid defaults component-sensitive; list/attribute/package wrappers dispatched. Full FilterItemStack244 read but underlying ItemAttribute, PackageItem matchAddress, GenericItemEmptying, ItemHelper.sameItem and external ItemStack codec not deep audited; no all variant equivalence or corrupt-payload safety claim.",
    "No cargo consumption/payment/quest/reward performed; this is durable authored world gameplay policy, not permanent player growth. Overlapping trains overwrite single currentTrain last keepAlive; no multi-occupancy event queue or exactly-once notification. Optional ComputerCraft only callsite read, no actual peripheral event delivery/ACK validation.",
    "Ordinary graph read does not call blockEntityAdded when binding existing UUID, so graph logical filter and physical BE copy may disagree after partial save. Behaviour read does not call filter callback. No atomic transaction among block/BE/global graph/train cargo data. Setter changes BE dirty; TrackObserver filter/count mutation has no direct graph dirty. Active Train.tick marks SavedData dirty; empty/no-train world policy edit save not guaranteed until another dirty event. No disk flush/durable ACK audited.",
    "Topology migration data cleared before point coexist/merge failure checks. Incompatible point can therefore lose migration payload. New observer blockEntityAdded deliberately restores physical BE filter over saved logical predicate. SingleBlockEntityEdgePoint disallows merge; wrong/missing track can postpone retry only before cleared point-creation section. Shared invalidation helpers are not new credit.",
    "Unknown edge point type skipped in EdgeData; malformed ResourceLocation or UUID not guarded. Base edge/distance/node/dimension not validated, missingdimension uses palette decode(-1), helper Catnip implementations uncached/not deep read. OccupiedObservers missingpoint skipped, not removed by tick loop; no delayed tombstone retention guarantee. Persisted arbitrary counters or stale occupancy can create residual output.",
    "FilteringBehaviour FilterAmount==0 migration resets amount/max and UpTo but this count is not used by cargo predicate, so no separate quantity migration credit. External user filter packet/screen and actual item placement debit not traced; registered item/factory and server callback are concrete producer only.",
    "Only listed ranges read; full Train/Carriage/GlobalRailwayManager/TrackTargeting/SmartBlockEntity classes not claimed. No actual current pack acceptance and no building reference credit."
  ],
